=== Prompt ===
Who is Darth Vader?

=== Response ===
Darth Vader, also known as Anakin Skywalker, is a central character in the Star Wars franchise. He was a Jedi Knight who played a significant role in the Clone Wars, but he eventually turned to the dark side of the Force and became a powerful Sith Lord.

Anakin Skywalker was a young slave boy who was discovered to be strong in the Force. He was freed by Jedi Master Qui-Gon Jinn and became a Padawan learner under Obi-Wan Kenobi. During the Clone Wars, Anakin became increasingly disillusioned with the Jedi Order and its restrictions on his power and freedom. He was seduced by the dark side by Palpatine, the Supreme Chancellor of the Galactic Republic, who promised to teach him the power to save Padmé Amidala, Anakin's secret wife.

Anakin's fall to the dark side was complete when he turned against the Jedi and pledged his allegiance to Palpatine. He was rebranded as Darth Vader, a powerful Sith Lord, and became a key figure in the execution of Order 66, which led to the near-destruction of the Jedi Order.

As Darth Vader, he served the Galactic Empire, carrying out the will of Emperor Palpatine and enforcing his rule through fear and intimidation. Vader's iconic appearance, including his black armor and breathing mask, has become synonymous with the character.

However, in the final film of the original trilogy, "Return of the Jedi," Vader undergoes a redemption arc, ultimately sacrificing himself to save his son, Luke Skywalker, and help bring balance to the Force. His legacy as a complex and conflicted character continues to fascinate audiences and inspire new interpretations and reimaginings in the Star Wars universe.

